==German Low German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fœ͡ɐ/|lang=nds-de}}

===Etymology 1===
Cognate to {{etyl|de|-}} [[für]].

====Alternative forms====
* [[vor]] {{qualifier|Low Prussian}}

====Preposition====
{{head|nds-de|preposition}}

# {{context|in some dialects, including|_|East Frisian|lang=nds-de}} [[for]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Authors who imitate or mimic German orthography spell this preposition ''för'' (like German ''für''), but the following preposition (meaning "in front of") ''vör'' (like German ''vor'').

===Etymology 2===
Cognate to {{etyl|de|-}} [[vor]].

====Alternative forms====
* [[vär]], [[veer]] ([[ver]]) {{qualifier|Low Prussian|lang=nds-de}}

====Preposition====
{{head|nds-de|preposition}}

# {{context|in some dialects|lang=nds-de}} [[in front of]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Authors who imitate or mimic German orthography spell this preposition ''vör'' (like German ''vor''), but the preceding preposition ''för'' (like German ''für'').

